      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Annular pancreas is a developmental anomaly that can be associated with other conditions such as Down syndrome, duodenal atresia, and Hirschsprung disease. A band of pancreatic tissue, in continuity with the pancreatic head, completely or incompletely encircles the descending duodenum, sometimes assuming a \"crocodile jaw\" configuration. We present the case of an adult who presented with epigastric pain and vomiting and was found to have annular pancreas."},
